ated"},{"text":" version","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of the actor, allowing synchronous access to actor local state without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hopping through asynchronous boundaries."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the current context is not running on the actor’s serial executor, or"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"if the actor is a reference to a remote actor, this method will crash"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a fatal error (similar to ","type":"text"},{"code":"preconditionIsolated()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that this check is performed against the passed in actor’s serial","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"executor, meaning that if another actor uses the same serial executor–by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using that actor’s "},{"code":"Actor\/unownedExecutor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Actor\/unownedExecutor"},{"text":"–this check will succeed, as from a concurrency","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"safety perspective, the serial executor guarantees mutual exclusion of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those two actors."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method can only be used from synchronous functions, as asynchronous"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"functions should instead perform a normal method call to the actor, which","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"will hop task execution to the target actor if necessary.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This check is performed against the actor’s serial executor,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text"